<title>USA: US weekly soybean crush 24,386,000 bushels -- NOPA.</title>
<headline>US weekly soybean crush 24,386,000 bushels -- NOPA.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>National Oilseed Processors Association weekly soybean crushings by reporting members (crushings/capacity in bu, soymeal exports in short tons):</p>
<p>			 07/02/97    06/25/97	Year-Ago</p>
<p> Crushings	 24,386,000  24,223,000    26,839,000</p>
<p> Meal Exports	  95,056	65,334	     N/A</p>
<p> Capacity-X	35,451,000  35,451,000    34,100,000</p>
<p> Capacity-Y	35,643,944  35,643,944	     N/A</p>
<p>X-Members reporting weekly. Y-Weekly reporters plus members reporting only monthly. N/A-Not Available. Totals may not agree due to rounding by NOPA. R-revised  </p>
<p>NOPA reported the following soybean crushings and capacity use by state for the week, with comparisons, in bushels:</p>
<p>    CRUSHINGS --   07/02/97    06/25/97     Year-Ago</p>
<p> Illinois	   4,338,000   4,399,000     4,534,000</p>
<p> Ind,Ky,Ohio,Mich 4,276,000   4,507,000     4,268,000</p>
<p> Southeast	  4,010,000   3,612,000     4,633,000</p>
<p> South Central    1,865,000   1,910,000     2,780,000</p>
<p> Southwest	  3,363,000   3,370,000     3,707,000</p>
<p> Iowa		 4,638,000   4,369,000     4,970,000</p>
<p> Minn,ND,SD,Mont  1,895,000   2,054,000     1,947,000</p>
<p> Total U.S.	24,386,000  24,223,000    26,839,000</p>
